      "file": "app/controllers/redirects_controller.rb",
      "line": 7,
      "note": "Redirecting to a user-supplied external URL is the entire purpose of a URL shortener, so allow_other_host is intentional here. The risk Brakeman flags -- redirecting to a hostile scheme -- is handled at write time instead: UrlValidator restricts Link#url to absolute http/https URLs with a host, so javascript:, data: and file: URLs can never be persisted and therefore can never be redirected to. See spec/models/link_spec.rb for the coverage."
